  "verbalization": "Mitomycin is linked to NBsusSR through a series of target relationships that involve bromodomain-containing proteins and lysine-specific demethylases. The evidence suggests that mitomycin acts as a target for multiple compounds, including palmarumycin CP18 and [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which in turn target NBsusSR. These compounds are likely involved in epigenetic regulation, as they are demethylase inhibitors, and their interaction with NBsusSR may be mediated through these enzymes. The presence of multiple pathways connecting mitomycin to NBsusSR highlights a potential mechanism involving epigenetic modulation, where mitomycin indirectly influences NBsusSR through its effects on these enzymes. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the role of bromodomain-containing proteins and demethylase inhibitors in mediating the interaction between mitomycin and NBsusSR.",
